{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01B9H8oZ5tgFCUGHw5RyppMM","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tid: srd085-sync\n2\ttitle: \"cmd/sync: Synchronize Cached Writes to Persistent Storage\"\n3\t\n4\tproblem: |\n5\t  macOS ships sync but the GNU version supports --data and --file-system flags for\n6\t  selective synchronization. The Go implementation must match the Homebrew GNU reference\n7\t  binary (gsync, installed by coreutils) byte-for-byte on all flag combinations, verified\n8\t  by differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n9\t\n10\tgoals:\n11\t  - G1: Synchronize cached writes to persistent storage.\n12\t  - G2: Support per-file and filesystem-level sync options.\n13\t  - G3: Verify functional parity against gsync via differential testing.\n14\t\n15\trequirements:\n16\t  R1:\n17\t    title: Synchronization modes\n18\t    items:\n19\t      - R1.1:\n20\t          text: When invoked with no arguments, must call sync(2) to flush all filesystem caches to persistent storage.\n21\t      - R1.2:\n22\t          text: When given FILE arguments, must open each file and call fsync(2) on each to flush that file's data and metadata to storage.\n23\t      - R1.3:\n24\t          text: \"-d or --data must call fdatasync(2) instead of fsync(2) on each FILE, syncing only the file's data (not metadata). Must exit 1 if no FILE is given with -d.\"\n25\t      - R1.4:\n26\t          text: \"-f or --file-system must call sync(2) for the filesystem containing each FILE rather than syncing the individual file. Must exit 1 if no FILE is given with -f.\"\n27\t\n28\t  R2:\n29\t    title: Exit codes and SIGPIPE\n30\t    items:\n31\t      - R2.1:\n32\t          text: Must exit 0 when all sync operations complete successfully.\n33\t      - R2.2:\n34\t          text: Must exit 1 when any file cannot be opened or sync fails.\n35\t      - R2.3:\n36\t          text: Must handle SIGPIPE gracefully (exit 0) using pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler.\n37\t\n38\tnon_goals:\n39\t  - cmd/sync does not implement filesystem-type-specific sync semantics beyond what the OS provides.\n40\t\n41\tacceptance_criteria:\n42\t  - id: AC1\n43\t    criterion: \"sync with no arguments completes without error, matching gsync.\"\n44\t    traces:\n45\t      - R1.1\n46\t  - id: AC2\n47\t    criterion: \"sync file flushes the file to storage, matching gsync file.\"\n48\t    traces:\n49\t      - R1.2\n50\t  - id: AC3\n51\t    criterion: \"Differential test against gsync passes for all required test cases.\"\n52\t    traces:\n53\t      - R1.1\n54\t      - R1.2\n55\t      - R1.3\n56\t      - R1.4\n57\t  - id: AC4\n58\t    criterion: \"cmd/sync compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n59\t    traces:\n60\t      - R1.1\n61\t      - R1.2\n62\t      - R1.3\n63\t      - R1.4\n64\t      - R2.1\n65\t      - R2.2\n66\t      - R2.3\n67\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"32d25cb8-d0bd-458b-866d-1aa82465e655","uuid":"fe00f36c-59f0-4112-89ac-091c40ccd609","timestamp":"2026-05-23T12:39:29.750Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5530/docs/specs/software-requirements/srd085-sync.yaml","content":"id: srd085-sync\ntitle: \"cmd/sync: Synchronize Cached Writes to Persistent Storage\"\n\nproblem: |\n  macOS ships sync but the GNU version supports --data and --file-system flags for\n  selective synchronization. The Go implementation must match the Homebrew GNU reference\n  binary (gsync, installed by coreutils) byte-for-byte on all flag combinations, verified\n  by differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n\ngoals:\n  - G1: Synchronize cached writes to persistent storage.\n  - G2: Support per-file and filesystem-level sync options.\n  - G3: Verify functional parity against gsync via differential testing.\n\nrequirements:\n  R1:\n    title: Synchronization modes\n    items:\n      - R1.1:\n          text: When invoked with no arguments, must call sync(2) to flush all filesystem caches to persistent storage.\n      - R1.2:\n          text: When given FILE arguments, must open each file and call fsync(2) on each to flush that file's data and metadata to storage.\n      - R1.3:\n          text: \"-d or --data must call fdatasync(2) instead of fsync(2) on each FILE, syncing only the file's data (not metadata). Must exit 1 if no FILE is given with -d.\"\n      - R1.4:\n          text: \"-f or --file-system must call sync(2) for the filesystem containing each FILE rather than syncing the individual file. Must exit 1 if no FILE is given with -f.\"\n\n  R2:\n    title: Exit codes and SIGPIPE\n    items:\n      - R2.1:\n          text: Must exit 0 when all sync operations complete successfully.\n      - R2.2:\n          text: Must exit 1 when any file cannot be opened or sync fails.\n      - R2.3:\n          text: Must handle SIGPIPE gracefully (exit 0) using pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler.\n\nnon_goals:\n  - cmd/sync does not implement filesystem-type-specific sync semantics beyond what the OS provides.\n\nacceptance_criteria:\n  - id: AC1\n    criterion: \"sync with no arguments completes without error, matching gsync.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n  - id: AC2\n    criterion: \"sync file flushes the file to storage, matching gsync file.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.2\n  - id: AC3\n    criterion: \"Differential test against gsync passes for all required test cases.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R1.4\n  - id: AC4\n    criterion: \"cmd/sync compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R1.4\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R2.3\n","numLines":67,"startLine":1,"totalLines":67}}}
